"1598",""
"1599","Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, said: ""I came with my masters intending to migrate until we drew near to Medina. They entered Medina and left me behind them. Severe hunger afflicted me. Some people leaving Medina passed by me and said to me: 'If you entered the city, you could eat from the fruit of its gardens.' So I entered a garden and cut from two date clusters. The owner of the garden came to me and brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and informed him of my story. I was wearing two garments. He said to me: 'Which of them is better?' I pointed to one of them. He said: 'Take it and give the other to the owner of the garden,' and he let me go free."""
"1600",""
"1601",""
"1602",""
